senses.gloss:
सम + -दुःख a. feeling for anotherʼs woe, sympathising (with another);
 a fellow-sufferer; Ku. 4. 4. ˚सुख a. a companion or partner in
 joy and sorrow; पृष्टा जनेन समदुःखसुखेन बाला Ś. 3. 10.

समक्ष + .{@-क्षम्@} ind. In the presence of, visibly, before the very eyes;
 तथा समक्षं दहता मनोभवम् Ku. 5. 1.
.━{@Comp.@}: समक्षदर्शनम्

समर्थ + .{@-र्थः@}
—1 A significant word (in gram.); अव्ययं समर्थेन सह समस्यते सोऽव्ययीभावः Sk.
—2 The coherence of words together in a significant sentence.

समर्थ + .{@-र्थम्@}
—1 Ability, competence.
—2 Intelligibility.

समापन्न + .{@-न्नम्@}
—1 End, completion.
—2 Death.

समाप्तिक + .{@-कः@}
—1 A finisher.
—2 One who has completed the whole course of holy studies; Ms. 3. 145.

समीक्षः + .{@-क्षम्@}
—1 Complete investigation.
—2 The Sāṃkhya system of philosophy.

समीचीन + .{@-नम्@}
—1 Truth.
—2 Propriety.

समुदयः + .{@-यम्@}
—1 The rising of a planet &c.
—2 An auspicious moment (लग्न).

सामवायिक + .{@-कः@}
—1 A minister, counsellor.
—2 The chief of a company or corporation.
